<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφύομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φύσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.Jun.
					<u>Im.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			: with aor. 2
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διέφῡν</span>: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπέφῡκα</span>:—<i>germinate,</i> of seeds,
				<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.17.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be disjoined,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφύντος ἑνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					17.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>grow between,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				335
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.7.9
			</span></i>; <i>intervene,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος διέφυ καὶ πάντα ἐξήρτυτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.61
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαθὺς δ. αὐλών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eratosth.
					8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>to be different from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ἀλλήλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			<i>to be inseparably connected with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.Jun.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; <i>to identify oneself with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Dio</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be intimately acquainted with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Ἑλληνικῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					72.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				77.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ὅλης τῆς Ἰταλίας</span>
			<i>to pervade, leaven</i> all Italy (of Sulla's veterans), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> only metri gr., <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> l. c.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
